WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.400
Hi everyone,

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.301
welcome to Imseriou!

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.469
This is a channel dedicated to saving

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:03.503
the wallets of all male boyfriends

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.871
and husbands.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:05.839
Do you often hear

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:07.307
your partner say things like, "

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:08.141
I'm going abroad,

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.476
I'm going to the duty-free shop to buy that

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:10.543
bag! That bag is so cheap!

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.578
It's made

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:12.579
in Italy! I'm in Italy

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.114
, it would be such a

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:15.281
waste

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.649
if I didn't buy a bag to take back!"

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:17.650
But in this episode, I'm going to tell you

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.519
that many of those expensive designer bags

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.854
are actually made in Taichung.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.656
Remember that episode we filmed about

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.191
how factories recycle plastic bottles and other

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:25.992
waste materials

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.060
to make clothes

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.095
and other woven fabrics

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.131
? That's why so many girls go crazy seeing

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:31.898
Burberry , Mars

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:33.199
, Marc Jacobs, and other

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:34.300
designer brands.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.036
(Still don't understand)

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:37.404
You might not be able to pronounce the names of these things

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:38.805
, but your girlfriend definitely will.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:39.873
And these expensive items

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:40.874
actually have their webbing

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:41.875
made in Taichung.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:44.210
Like the CK

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.178
belts that many people like to buy

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.981
, the COACH belts you buy at duty-free shops abroad

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:49.482
, or the dog leashes you use

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.650
to walk your Chihuahua

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.252
, and even many military supplies used by

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.220
the National Revolutionary Army during drills—

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.655
as long as they are extremely strong,

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:56.456
durable

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:57.690
, and functional, and you can

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.625
wear them to show off,

00:00:58.625 --> 00:00:59.426
this

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:00.894
high-standard production

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:01.895
is all from this company.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.663
But why did the predecessor of this brand-name bag

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.032
company make military supplies?

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.067
This all goes back to

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.234
the Flying Tigers.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.169
"Hong Kong Flag Soldiers

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:09.969
"—no, it's not

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.204
the Flying Tigers .

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.639
"Hong Kong Flag Soldiers" refers to the era of Ng Man-tat

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.174
. Do you know the Flying Tigers?

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:15.608
When we used to play GTA, we

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.876
usually... If you're a five-star

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.144
Flying Tiger, they'll come and arrest you.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:18.912
But did you know that the Flying Tigers

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.647
were actually the Kuomintang

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:21.548
army during that time?

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.383
So, not everything that flies down from the sky is called the Flying Tigers.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.585
There are many types of armies that fly down from the sky,

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:26.953
one of which is the Flying Tigers.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.555
And today, we're

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:29.689
not in a temple

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:30.757
, but in a factory.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:31.491
This factory

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.159
is closely related to the Flying Tigers.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.427
Why are there chickens there?

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.898
This company has a very unique style.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:40.700
It has

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.102
the atmosphere left by the early Kuomintang government

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:44.304
, while also having modern factory automation

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.306
, Italian and Swiss machinery

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:48.808
, and traditional Taiwanese architecture

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.910
, including the former owner's dormitory.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.778
And this owner

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:52.579
actually

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.380
came to Taiwan with the Flying Tigers.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.515
I don't know if you've heard of them

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:56.416
, but in the early days,

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:57.117
there was a group of

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.017
Mainlanders

00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.819
who came with the Kuomintang government. One of the groups that

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.454
came to Taiwan was the Flying Tigers. Why are

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.322
the Flying Tigers

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:03.823
so legendary?

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.091
Back then, they came to Taiwan

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.793
to produce military equipment,

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.294
and now they make bags that let women

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.829
show off their firepower.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.164
To understand this, we need to start from the beginning.

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:11.965
In

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.933
the 1940s,

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.202
when

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.103
the Nationalist government

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:19.706
was still on the Chinese mainland battlefield,

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.541
a group of fighter planes flew overhead.

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:22.842
Japanese pilots

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.177
would skip a beat

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:26.346
whenever they saw that paint scheme.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:27.714
That was the P-40

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:28.781
Afghan fighter plane

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.884
with its gaping shark mouth on the nose

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:31.384
. Yes ,

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:32.051
that's the Flying Tigers.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:32.752
Unbelievable, right?

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:33.219
To be honest,

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.922
the P-40 wasn't the most powerful fighter plane at the time

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:36.422
, but

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.558
it had a design that will always be unforgettable

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:39.425
: that fierce,

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.060
fanged shark mouth paint scheme.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.762
Did you know...? Do you know how this design came about?

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:43.329
One day,

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.531
a Flying Tigers member

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:46.199
saw a picture of the Australian P-40 in a magazine

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:46.633
and exclaimed

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:47.567
, "Look, that's cool!" He

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:48.735
then reported this to his superiors.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:49.702
His purpose was simple

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.304
: to intimidate the Japanese.

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.639
But something interesting happened

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:54.174
. You know, in the 1940s,

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:55.108
the people of Kunming

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.743
had never seen a shark in their lives.

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:58.011
There

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:58.845
were no

00:02:58.845 --> 00:02:59.879
zoos or aquariums back then,

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:00.980
and Kunming

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:01.748
was very far from the sea.

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.082
So when they

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:03.850
saw this fighter plane,

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:04.617
their first reaction was,

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.352
"Wow, look

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.220
! It

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.121
's a winged tiger

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.856
flying in the sky!"

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:10.957
So

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.425
, this

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:13.226
story

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.295
spread like wildfire, and

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:16.796
the name " Flying

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:17.564
Tiger"

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:18.765
was born. Tiger,

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:20.300
so the direct Chinese translation of this team

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.501
is "Flying Tigers,"

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.436
hence

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.370
the name of the Flying Tigers team

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.471
. Unexpected,

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.039
right?

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.240
So, you see this over

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.141
here,

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.676
you might think it's a temple for the Flying Tigers?

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:30.710
No,

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:31.811
look inside,

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:32.512
this is... what is this

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:34.547
?

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.149
The Flying Tigers' staff canteen!

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:36.583
No,

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.117
it's their company's staff canteen!

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.052
Before entering, you have to say

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.954
"Dear, sincere,"

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:41.788
but this isn't

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:42.622
it. This is a factory

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:43.423
, a factory in Taichung.

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:44.390
So, that's right,

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.793
today we're not taking you to

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:48.494
an old military dependents' village

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:49.429
, but a factory

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:51.364
—a factory that makes many brand-name bags.

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.098
My grandfather, for example

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:53.399
, was a mainlander who

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.201
had to come to Taiwan because of the war.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.502
But my grandfather

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.870
was a policeman back then

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:58.571
.

00:03:58.571 --> 00:03:59.572
He loved

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.040
sitting in this pavilion. Here

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.208
, while brewing tea,

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:03.243
he recounts

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.477
the story of how his grandfather was shot several times

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:05.912
by the Communists.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.280
You know, my grandfather really did have

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.982
Communist bullets in his back

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:10.483
. I'll share that story on the members' channel

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.351
since

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:11.985
members can't participate

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:14.454
in this group buy for designer bags

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:16.456
. Back then, the Flying Tigers general

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:17.023
wondered

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:18.157
how to make the Flying Tigers

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:19.792
a highly loyal and courageous

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:20.760
force

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.895
that could attract strong pilots.

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:24.797
At that time, the average US Army pilot earned

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:27.033
about $347 a month, which

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:27.934
was a very high

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.002
salary in those days.

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:31.437
So, the Flying Tigers general

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:32.772
came up with a

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:33.940
very effective method

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:34.774
because he believed that

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.309
relying solely on patriotism

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:36.943
wouldn't work.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.278
Do you know what method he used? Did

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:39.979
he distribute a $10,000 bonus to everyone

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:40.613
?

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.448
He used

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:43.750
the most effective method in the last century

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.084
: a hefty reward will surely attract brave men.

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:46.653
He offered $600

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:48.721
to attract many fearless pilots.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.990
Then, for every Japanese plane shot down,

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.859
you could receive an additional $500.

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.060
Do you know

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.229
how much that $347 was worth?

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:56.829
Back then,

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.865
it was roughly equivalent

00:04:58.865 --> 00:04:59.799
to a down payment on a house

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:00.667
in the United States.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.068
You see how expensive down payments were in Taiwan

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:03.503
! This reward system

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:04.804
attracted

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.739
hundreds of pilots

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.107
and over 200 ground crew members

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:09.842
to join the Nationalist government's army,

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:10.710
specifically the Flying Tigers.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:11.244
That's why

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:12.679
people talk about... When people talked about the Flying Tigers,

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:14.147
they thought that besides being very good fighters,

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.682
they were also very wealthy.

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:16.649
If you're

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:18.117
a military enthusiast,

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.118
when you hear about the Flying Tigers,

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.053
you'll definitely think of something

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:20.820
called a "blood

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.121
banner." What was this blood banner for?

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:23.990
Back then,

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.825
any foreigner stationed in Greater China

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:27.393
could produce this blood banner

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:28.995
, and regardless of skin color

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:29.962
,

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:32.432
everyone would stand together through thick

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:33.099
and thin.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:34.934
It would bear the flag of the Republic of China

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.436
and the twelve large characters:

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:37.937
"Foreigners stationed in China, military

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:39.405
and civilians united, rescue and relief.

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:40.139
" Now, let Ray

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:41.708
try this blood banner in America.

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:43.209
Of course, with the end of the war,

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:44.110
the Flying Tigers...

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.346
It started as a military fighter jet unit

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:47.680
and then transformed into this

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:48.848
CAT transport team

00:05:48.848 --> 00:05:51.017
. The members of this CAT transport team are the boss,

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:51.918
Chairman Guo Huanmin,

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.353
whom we've been talking about

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:54.087
for

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:54.821
so long.

00:05:54.821 --> 00:05:57.557
The country has its principles and the army has its discipline; military

00:05:57.557 --> 00:06:00.126
discipline is the lifeblood of the army.

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:02.161
Behind this tea-drinking area

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:03.796
is Chairman Guo

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:04.697
's

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:05.465
former home.

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.400
He used to live next to the factory.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.735
And do you know what

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:09.635
the factory was called

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.170
? Zhongxing Textile Manufacturing.

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:14.307
So, the "loyalty" in his name

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:15.441
is

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:16.776
the kind of loyalty you'd

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:18.010
expect. You mean the heart, right

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:18.511
?

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:19.045
No, it

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:20.113
's the "prosperity" in "prosperity

00:06:20.113 --> 00:06:20.713
"—a pun on the word

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:21.781
"loyalty. " Their pun back then

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:22.815
came from the word "loyalty."

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:24.016
Loyalty without reservation

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.551
is like the concept of the Flying Tigers. Patriotic loyalty alone is useless. Besides

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:27.987
loyalty,

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:29.188
for

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:30.623
your factory to prosper

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:31.524
, it also

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:32.859
needs to be happy.

00:06:32.859 --> 00:06:33.926
If the factory isn't prosperous,

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:35.027
how can the chickens crow?

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:37.730
Okay, we've talked so much,

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:40.299
and now we know the background of this company.

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:41.434
So now we're going inside.

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:42.235
Have you all learned

00:06:42.235 --> 00:06:43.970
enough about this factory? But

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:45.905
you still don't understand

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:47.740
how military belts

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.342
, Armani webbing

00:06:49.342 --> 00:06:51.377
, CK fabric tape, and

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:51.878
COACH tape

00:06:51.878 --> 00:06:52.478
are made

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:53.880
. Let's go inside the factory!

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:54.680
To make

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:55.415
this

00:06:55.415 --> 00:06:56.482
easier for everyone to read,

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:58.050
we'll be showing you

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:58.785
a factory tour

00:06:58.785 --> 00:06:59.986
with simultaneous filming

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:00.753
and narration.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:02.522
First, we'll begin with raw material preparation,

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:03.856
the

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:04.424
so-called yarn stage.

00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:05.591
The factory needs to purchase

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:06.692
and prepare various

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:08.227
raw yarns for webbing.

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:08.795
Different yarns have different

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:09.529
counts, so they

00:07:09.529 --> 00:07:11.097
'll be first processed by combining them –

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:12.265
we discussed this in the previous episode,

00:07:12.265 --> 00:07:13.065
so we won't go into detail.

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:14.400
The main purpose of this step

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.935
is to make the yarn more viscous.

00:07:15.935 --> 00:07:17.470
Next, the yarn is woven into

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.138
loops and lengths

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:21.207
to create skeins.

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:22.542
After skeining,

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:23.543
we move on to the

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:24.811
dyeing and finishing process.

00:07:24.811 --> 00:07:25.645
The purpose of this is

00:07:25.645 --> 00:07:27.146
to give each brand's bags

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:28.781
their company color. Or perhaps it's

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:29.982
a new color scheme they're launching

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:31.284
this season

00:07:31.284 --> 00:07:32.552
, so the color you see

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:33.653
isn't actually printed on

00:07:33.653 --> 00:07:34.654
; every thread

00:07:34.654 --> 00:07:35.555
is that color.

00:07:35.555 --> 00:07:36.556
The thread is made

00:07:36.556 --> 00:07:37.990
by dyeing it this way.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:38.591
But

00:07:38.591 --> 00:07:40.193
if the color isn't right after dyeing and finishing

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:41.160
, you can't deliver.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.095
Or, if you only discover it's been rejected

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:44.330
when you're finally weaving the ribbon,

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:45.298
you're doomed.

00:07:45.298 --> 00:07:47.166
So, even if you're in manufacturing,

00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:48.534
whether it's footwear, fabric

00:07:48.534 --> 00:07:50.069
, or many other industries , if

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:51.471
you don't precisely correct

00:07:51.471 --> 00:07:53.406
every step,

00:07:53.406 --> 00:07:54.540
you're truly doomed

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.309
when you send it overseas

00:07:56.309 --> 00:07:57.443
or when the final product comes out.

00:07:57.443 --> 00:07:57.810
Of course,

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.345
you see some designer bags

00:07:59.345 --> 00:08:01.013
or... Many big brands

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:02.849
may have the same color

00:08:02.849 --> 00:08:04.417
, but the materials are different.

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:05.818
They may be nylon

00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:07.086
, yarn, or cotton.

00:08:07.086 --> 00:08:09.889
The difficulty lies in

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:11.357
achieving the same

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:12.458
color intensity and hue in the final dyeing.

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:14.360
Because even with different materials,

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.962
the dyeing methods for

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:17.930
achieving the same green

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:18.998
, blue, or red

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:20.199
are completely different

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:21.667
, but the final result

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:22.935
must look the same .

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:24.303
And look at the material behind me,

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:25.605
what is it?

00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:26.472
Kelp .

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:27.573
Kelp and

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:28.474
nylon

00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:29.075
.

00:08:29.075 --> 00:08:30.276
The dyeing and finishing method for nylon

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:31.310
does not require high temperature

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:32.278
; room temperature dyeing

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:33.746
is sufficient . What happens after dyeing?

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:35.114
Just like after washing clothes, if

00:08:35.114 --> 00:08:36.249
the clothes are stained,

00:08:36.249 --> 00:08:36.883
you still need to

00:08:36.883 --> 00:08:37.383
dehydrate them.

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:38.885
So, we move on to the dehydration step

00:08:40.086 --> 00:08:41.287
. How does it spin-dry?

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:42.655
It's like washing clothes.

00:08:42.655 --> 00:08:44.123
You just throw your clothes in

00:08:44.123 --> 00:08:45.224
, cover them,

00:08:45.224 --> 00:08:46.425
and it starts spinning.

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:47.493
After spinning,

00:08:47.493 --> 00:08:48.694
you can tumble

00:08:48.694 --> 00:08:49.462
dry.

00:08:49.462 --> 00:08:50.496
But some materials

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:51.264
can be tumble dried

00:08:51.264 --> 00:08:52.498
, while others don't,

00:08:52.498 --> 00:08:53.900
just like washing clothes.

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:54.867
If it's cotton

00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:55.701
, you can tumble dry

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:56.802
; if it's nylon ,

00:08:56.802 --> 00:08:57.670
you don't need to tumble dry;

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:58.938
or if it's polyester, you

00:08:58.938 --> 00:08:59.739
don't need to tumble dry either.

00:08:59.739 --> 00:09:01.107
But sometimes,

00:09:01.107 --> 00:09:02.742
like when you work hard

00:09:02.742 --> 00:09:04.076
and don't earn much money

00:09:04.076 --> 00:09:04.911
, but your girlfriend

00:09:04.911 --> 00:09:05.645
or partner

00:09:05.645 --> 00:09:06.879
keeps nagging you to buy bags

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:07.813
, you can tell her,

00:09:07.813 --> 00:09:08.548
"Go tumble dry."

00:09:08.781 --> 00:09:10.182
Did you see that auntie in there?

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:10.917
She

00:09:10.917 --> 00:09:12.051
works in a textile factory.

00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:12.785
Do you know what she is,

00:09:12.785 --> 00:09:13.419
boss

00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:14.253
?

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:16.756
She is the Weaver Girl who meets

00:09:16.756 --> 00:09:18.691
the Cowherd on the Qixi Festival.

00:09:18.691 --> 00:09:19.759
So...

00:09:19.759 --> 00:09:20.726
therefore, the Weaver Girl

00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:23.062
must have a Cowherd in her heart.

00:09:23.062 --> 00:09:24.597
Then the Cowherd

00:09:24.597 --> 00:09:26.032
will ask her

00:09:26.032 --> 00:09:26.632
if she wants to dry

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:28.034
the webbing. After

00:09:28.034 --> 00:09:29.101
drying, it is

00:09:29.769 --> 00:09:31.137
made into tubular

00:09:31.137 --> 00:09:32.905
yarn.

00:09:32.905 --> 00:09:33.973
Then it is warped.

00:09:33.973 --> 00:09:34.707
After warping,

00:09:34.707 --> 00:09:36.375
we will shape it into a large coil.

00:09:36.375 --> 00:09:37.243
But so far,

00:09:37.243 --> 00:09:38.544
you haven't started yet.

00:09:38.544 --> 00:09:39.879
You are just preparing .

00:09:39.879 --> 00:09:41.447
But why do you need to do all this preparation?

00:09:41.447 --> 00:09:42.848
Because if this part is not decided

00:09:42.848 --> 00:09:44.283
when the client and designer

00:09:44.283 --> 00:09:45.451
are in the development stage,

00:09:45.451 --> 00:09:46.886
it will become a disaster.

00:09:46.886 --> 00:09:48.087
What kind of pattern do you want to make?

00:09:48.087 --> 00:09:49.355
What kind of gradient do you want to make?

00:09:49.355 --> 00:09:50.623
At this time, your engineers

00:09:50.623 --> 00:09:53.092
have to carefully perform manual work.

00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:53.626
And this

00:09:53.626 --> 00:09:55.194
is

00:09:55.194 --> 00:09:55.861
the most important

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:56.429
, time-consuming

00:09:56.429 --> 00:09:58.598
and labor-intensive key technology in your finished product.

00:09:58.598 --> 00:10:00.833
After the materials and colors are ready,

00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:02.134
you can take the pattern you want

00:10:02.134 --> 00:10:03.669
and the design file

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:06.038
and start the weaving action.

00:10:06.038 --> 00:10:07.573
You can weave the shape you want

00:10:07.573 --> 00:10:08.574
and the pattern you want.

00:10:08.674 --> 00:10:09.175
Weaving

00:10:09.175 --> 00:10:10.543
can be thought of as

00:10:10.543 --> 00:10:12.144
starting to knit.

00:10:12.144 --> 00:10:13.646
In plain terms... In plain language,

00:10:13.646 --> 00:10:14.947
all the patterns you see

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:16.182
are

00:10:16.182 --> 00:10:17.316
created through the weaving process.

00:10:17.316 --> 00:10:18.584
The different interweaving

00:10:18.584 --> 00:10:19.685
and overlapping of

00:10:19.685 --> 00:10:20.820
warp and weft threads , whether

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.121
you want to weave across threads

00:10:22.121 --> 00:10:24.023
or meticulously weave each step

00:10:24.023 --> 00:10:25.191
, or what colors

00:10:25.191 --> 00:10:25.958
you want to combine

00:10:25.958 --> 00:10:26.892
—brown

00:10:26.892 --> 00:10:27.426
, black

00:10:27.426 --> 00:10:28.127
, gray—

00:10:28.127 --> 00:10:29.128
all these things happen

00:10:29.128 --> 00:10:31.464
during the weaving process.

00:10:31.464 --> 00:10:32.198
It sounds complicated

00:10:32.198 --> 00:10:33.165
, but don't worry,

00:10:33.165 --> 00:10:34.133
because now we have computers.

00:10:34.133 --> 00:10:35.601
Computers don't just select potatoes;

00:10:35.601 --> 00:10:36.535
they can weave fabric too.

00:10:36.535 --> 00:10:38.037
So, just put it on a production line,

00:10:38.037 --> 00:10:39.205
and you can produce

00:10:39.205 --> 00:10:40.673
all sorts of webbing,

00:10:40.673 --> 00:10:41.407
brands

00:10:41.407 --> 00:10:42.241
, and styles—

00:10:42.241 --> 00:10:43.476
underwear straps,

00:10:43.476 --> 00:10:44.110
gun straps—

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:45.344
almost 24/7 .

00:10:45.344 --> 00:10:45.778
Once the webbing is finished,

00:10:45.778 --> 00:10:47.013
you might think it's ready for delivery.

00:10:47.013 --> 00:10:47.680
No

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:49.515
, every factory has QC (Quality Control) procedures,

00:10:49.515 --> 00:10:51.350
and each factory's QC methods are slightly different.

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.351
How do factories

00:10:52.351 --> 00:10:53.152
that make designer bag

00:10:53.152 --> 00:10:54.186
webbing check QC

00:10:54.186 --> 00:10:56.455
? They check each piece slowly and meticulously

00:10:56.455 --> 00:10:58.557
from beginning to end.

00:10:58.557 --> 00:10:59.125
How do they

00:10:59.125 --> 00:11:00.059
check it manually,

00:11:00.059 --> 00:11:01.260
like this one?

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:01.794
Look,

00:11:01.794 --> 00:11:03.396
like this finished webbing,

00:11:03.396 --> 00:11:04.630
what do you check now?

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:06.032
First, the color;

00:11:06.032 --> 00:11:07.400
second, whether

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.235
there's anything next to it... Whether the thread is contaminated

00:11:09.235 --> 00:11:10.636
, suddenly skipped a stitch

00:11:10.636 --> 00:11:11.837
, or is missing

00:11:11.837 --> 00:11:13.239
, and then what do we need

00:11:13.239 --> 00:11:14.140
to measure the thickness at the end

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:14.874
, you'll understand why

00:11:14.874 --> 00:11:16.175
many luxury bags are so expensive

00:11:16.175 --> 00:11:16.876
. It's because

00:11:16.876 --> 00:11:18.010
many of their components

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:18.878
are actually damaged

00:11:18.878 --> 00:11:20.646
during the dyeing and finishing process

00:11:20.646 --> 00:11:22.882
, or accidentally contaminated

00:11:22.882 --> 00:11:24.050
, or the machine's

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:25.317
precision wasn't properly calibrated, causing the

00:11:25.317 --> 00:11:26.352
thread to suddenly

00:11:26.786 --> 00:11:27.720
skip a stitch

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:28.287
during production.

00:11:28.287 --> 00:11:29.755
You can already see the damage in this kind of thing.

00:11:29.755 --> 00:11:30.589
If you can't see it here

00:11:30.589 --> 00:11:31.057
, it means

00:11:31.057 --> 00:11:32.591
there was a mistake

00:11:32.591 --> 00:11:33.459
during the weaving process,

00:11:33.459 --> 00:11:34.360
so QC won't pass it.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:35.461
If you still can't see this,

00:11:35.461 --> 00:11:36.195
then it's this kind

00:11:36.195 --> 00:11:37.430
—at least you can see it now.

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:38.264
So, going back to the point,

00:11:38.264 --> 00:11:39.131
I don't know if you

00:11:39.131 --> 00:11:40.566
often see

00:11:40.566 --> 00:11:42.802
people selling very cheap luxury goods

00:11:42.802 --> 00:11:43.836
, but if you look closely,

00:11:43.836 --> 00:11:44.670
they might be very similar to

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:46.639
what you buy in a boutique

00:11:46.639 --> 00:11:48.340
, even if they use the same materials

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:50.643
, or they might be sourced from Southeast Asia, mainland China, or somewhere else through some strange connection

00:11:50.643 --> 00:11:51.343
.

00:11:51.343 --> 00:11:52.011
They

00:11:52.011 --> 00:11:53.312
can

00:11:53.312 --> 00:11:54.380
make

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:55.948
many

00:11:55.948 --> 00:11:56.849
of them look very

00:11:56.849 --> 00:11:59.418
similar, even to the real thing.

00:11:59.452 --> 00:12:00.453
But the factory we're filming today,

00:12:00.453 --> 00:12:02.321
of course, has its products manufactured by the genuine manufacturer...

00:12:02.321 --> 00:12:03.389
We won't film counterfeits;

00:12:03.389 --> 00:12:04.390
we disdain them.

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:05.224
This factory,

00:12:05.224 --> 00:12:06.992
besides making designer bags, also

00:12:06.992 --> 00:12:07.993
produces

00:12:07.993 --> 00:12:08.728
functional

00:12:08.728 --> 00:12:10.329
items. As

00:12:10.329 --> 00:12:11.964
someone who works at heights

00:12:11.964 --> 00:12:13.399
, or someone who loves 3M,

00:12:13.399 --> 00:12:14.700
you might

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:16.135
use those "intestinal loops."

00:12:16.135 --> 00:12:17.203
When working at heights,

00:12:17.203 --> 00:12:18.604
if you accidentally fall,

00:12:18.604 --> 00:12:20.639
they can catch your body

00:12:20.639 --> 00:12:21.841
and prevent you from

00:12:21.841 --> 00:12:23.309
falling further.

00:12:23.309 --> 00:12:24.777
These slightly elastic loops are

00:12:24.777 --> 00:12:26.645
what we call "intestinal loops

00:12:26.645 --> 00:12:28.080
," and they're made by this company.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:28.781
They used

00:12:28.781 --> 00:12:30.015
to do business with the military

00:12:30.015 --> 00:12:32.618
and can produce military weapons.

00:12:32.618 --> 00:12:34.019
Besides aesthetically pleasing items,

00:12:34.019 --> 00:12:35.588
they can also make functional ones.

00:12:35.588 --> 00:12:36.388
Therefore, in this episode,

00:12:36.388 --> 00:12:37.923
I strongly suggest that the Nationalist Army

00:12:37.923 --> 00:12:38.958
purchase from them.

00:12:38.958 --> 00:12:40.559
You know, our army

00:12:40.559 --> 00:12:41.227
riflemen

00:12:41.227 --> 00:12:43.028
often carry rifle slings.

00:12:43.028 --> 00:12:44.563
You have to sling them over your shoulder

00:12:44.563 --> 00:12:45.431
while running

00:12:45.431 --> 00:12:46.866
, or rescue your comrade

00:12:46.866 --> 00:12:47.566
and pull them up

00:12:47.566 --> 00:12:48.367
, or if you're

00:12:48.367 --> 00:12:49.168
bleeding from a bullet,

00:12:49.168 --> 00:12:50.336
you can remove the sling

00:12:50.336 --> 00:12:51.437
and use a tourniquet.

00:12:51.437 --> 00:12:52.805
We strongly suggest that

00:12:52.805 --> 00:12:53.906
the Nationalist Army replace

00:12:53.906 --> 00:12:55.574
their rifle slings with designer bag straps

00:12:55.574 --> 00:12:56.509
. CK Army,

00:12:56.509 --> 00:12:57.643
Armani Rifle Team

00:12:57.643 --> 00:12:58.277
, COACH.

00:12:58.277 --> 00:12:58.911
When the Dior

00:12:58.911 --> 00:13:00.346
Nationalist soldiers marched out

00:13:00.346 --> 00:13:01.714
, all the women went

00:13:01.714 --> 00:13:02.114
crazy.

00:13:02.114 --> 00:13:02.615
Wow,

00:13:02.615 --> 00:13:04.150
his suspender is Dior!

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:05.851
Wow, that's a Chanel gun suspender!

00:13:05.851 --> 00:13:06.952
The Nationalist soldiers' morale was high.

00:13:06.952 --> 00:13:08.087
But of course, such high-standard items

00:13:08.087 --> 00:13:09.121
have very high requirements.

00:13:09.121 --> 00:13:09.622
Let me show you

00:13:09.622 --> 00:13:10.890
how many things were destroyed today.

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:12.358
What you see here is

00:13:12.358 --> 00:13:13.592
thicker and not yet ready for shipment

00:13:13.592 --> 00:13:15.528
; the feel is stiffer and not yet ready for

00:13:15.528 --> 00:13:17.296
shipment . It's hard to the touch

00:13:17.296 --> 00:13:18.497
, not rough.

00:13:18.497 --> 00:13:19.231
Very strict,

00:13:19.231 --> 00:13:19.999
very rigorous.

00:13:19.999 --> 00:13:21.333
And there are some

00:13:21.333 --> 00:13:22.101
cut-out

00:13:22.101 --> 00:13:23.169
samples here

00:13:23.169 --> 00:13:25.538
, used for comparison.

00:13:25.538 --> 00:13:27.173
I don't know if you've ever felt

00:13:27.173 --> 00:13:28.440
this way when buying designer bags,

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:29.074
wondering

00:13:29.074 --> 00:13:31.210
which country you bought this bag in and

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:33.112
which country I bought this bag in,

00:13:33.112 --> 00:13:34.413
even though we look the same.

00:13:34.413 --> 00:13:35.881
But why does it feel slightly different to the touch?

00:13:35.881 --> 00:13:37.016
Even though both are authentic

00:13:37.016 --> 00:13:38.350
, it's because different factories,

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:39.518
different yarns

00:13:39.518 --> 00:13:41.320
, or different materials

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:42.421
sometimes result

00:13:42.421 --> 00:13:43.656
in

00:13:43.656 --> 00:13:45.291
very subtle, barely noticeable differences.

00:13:45.291 --> 00:13:47.092
Unless you're a seasoned expert,

00:13:47.092 --> 00:13:48.360
you won't be able to tell the difference.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:49.094
So you see,

00:13:49.094 --> 00:13:51.397
such a meticulous factory and

00:13:51.397 --> 00:13:52.097
brand , with

00:13:52.097 --> 00:13:54.066
its spirit of fierce competition

00:13:54.066 --> 00:13:56.135
and refined fashion sense

00:13:56.135 --> 00:13:58.370
, is bound to attract many brands

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:00.906
and receive numerous awards.

00:14:00.906 --> 00:14:02.708
This final showroom

00:14:02.708 --> 00:14:04.476
should convince your partner

00:14:04.476 --> 00:14:05.611
and girlfriend.

00:14:05.611 --> 00:14:06.545
In the showroom,

00:14:06.545 --> 00:14:07.479
you'll see

00:14:07.479 --> 00:14:08.814
just how many world-renowned brands

00:14:08.814 --> 00:14:10.249
this company has produced for, like

00:14:10.249 --> 00:14:11.150
Lululemon,

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:12.017
COACH

00:14:12.017 --> 00:14:12.852
, Armani

00:14:12.852 --> 00:14:13.886
, and Chloé.

00:14:13.886 --> 00:14:14.553
Of course, there are many brands behind

00:14:14.553 --> 00:14:15.788
Burberry

